    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6adbe3577078e5.02648009\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">In the final hours of the WoW: Forever Beta, Blizzard decided to go out with a bang, giving players fun and chaotic events throughout the world.<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><div class=\"markup-bluetweet exclude-units\" data-loading=\"true\"><span class=\"twitter-tweet-loading fa fa-circle-o-notch fa-spin fa-fw q0\"></span><a href=\"https://twitter.com/wowheadtweets/status/2113297144165896222\">Tweet #2113297144165896222</a></div></div><br><br>Players would first find a new NPC in front of capital cities, offering unique consumables such as fireworks, a scroll that increases your and others' speed around you, and a potion that increases experience gained by 200%.<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306445.jpg\" id=\"1306445\"><img width=\"700\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306445.jpg?maxWidth=700\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image border\" alt=\"Gabbi Goodwhistle WoW Forever\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; aspect-ratio: 1.7876 / 1; border-width: 2px;\"></a>&nbsp;</div><br><br>Players would also find world bosses in starting zones, ranging from Azuregos, \"Super\" Hogger, Voracious, Thunderaan, and Lord Kazzak!<br><br><div class=\"markup-grid exclude-units\" data-align=\"centered\" style=\"--markup-gridColumnBasis: 400px;\"><div class=\"\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306447.jpg\" id=\"1306447\"><img width=\"400\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306447.jpg?maxWidth=400\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image border\" alt=\"Azshara Crater\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; aspect-ratio: 1.78174 / 1; border-width: 2px;\"></a><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><i>Voracious</i></div></div><div class=\"\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306451.jpg\" id=\"1306451\"><img width=\"400\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306451.jpg?maxWidth=400\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image border\" alt=\"Horde starting area\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; aspect-ratio: 1.77778 / 1; border-width: 2px;\"></a><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><i>Super Hogger</i></div></div><div class=\"\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306448.jpg\" id=\"1306448\"><img width=\"400\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306448.jpg?maxWidth=400\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image border\" alt=\"Alliance starting area\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; aspect-ratio: 1.77652 / 1; border-width: 2px;\"></a><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><i>Thunderaan</i></div></div><div class=\"last\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306449.jpg\" id=\"1306449\"><img width=\"380\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306449.jpg?maxWidth=380\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image border\" alt=\"Unfinished area\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; aspect-ratio: 1.67947 / 1; border-width: 2px;\"></a><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><i>Azuregos</i></div></div></div><br><br>Defeating these world bosses gave players some familiar and powerful legendaries, including Sulfuras, Hand of Ragnaros, and Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker!<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><div class=\"markup-bluetweet exclude-units\" data-loading=\"true\"><span class=\"twitter-tweet-loading fa fa-circle-o-notch fa-spin fa-fw q0\"></span><a href=\"https://twitter.com/wowheadtweets/status/2113348047342326176\">Tweet #2113348047342326176</a></div></div><br><br>Along with getting these legendaries, players could also farm full Classic Tier 1 set bonuses and Molten Core weapons from mobs in every starter zone.<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306452.jpg\" id=\"1306452\"><img width=\"500\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306452.jpg?maxWidth=500\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image border\" alt=\"WoW Forever Hunter Tier 1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; aspect-ratio: 0.945634 / 1; border-width: 2px;\"></a></div><br><br>But it appears all of that wasn't enough, as Blizzard decided to re-release the contaminated boxes from the Wrath of the Lich King Scourge Event back in 2008, spreading the Scourge plague across Azeroth!<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><div class=\"wh-twitch exclude-units\" style=\"max-width: 640px; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;\"></div></div><br><br>The WoW: Forever beta was a massive success, and players can't wait to jump back into Azeroth on November 4th. We'll see what other surprises are in store for us at launch!</div>\n            \n            <noscript>In the final hours of the WoW: Forever Beta, Blizzard decided to go out with a bang, giving players fun and chaotic events throughout the world.<br /><br />Players would first find a new NPC in front of capital cities, offering unique consumables such as fireworks, a scroll that increases your and others' speed around you, and a potion that increases experience gained by 200%.<br /><br />Players would also find world bosses in starting zones, ranging from Azuregos, &quot;Super&quot; Hogger, Voracious, Thunderaan, and Lord Kazzak!<br /><br /><i>Voracious</i><br /><br /><i>Super Hogger</i><br /><br /><i>Thunderaan</i><br /><br /><i>Azuregos</i><br /><br />Defeating these world bosses gave players some familiar and powerful legendaries, including Sulfuras, Hand of Ragnaros, and Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker!<br /><br />Along with getting these legendaries, players could also farm full Classic Tier 1 set bonuses and Molten Core weapons from mobs in every starter zone.<br /><br />But it appears all of that wasn't enough, as Blizzard decided to re-release the contaminated boxes from the Wrath of the Lich King Scourge Event back in 2008, spreading the Scourge plague across Azeroth!<br /><br />The WoW: Forever beta was a massive success, and players can't wait to jump back into Azeroth on November 4th. We'll see what other surprises are in store for us at launch!</noscript>            \n        ",
